WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.400
If you’re anything like me,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.560
you have lots of ambitious
plans for the future.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.160
I’ve got a whole series of
new books I want to write,

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.400
thousands more
videos to script.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.360
But guess what?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.760
None of us may be able to do
any of the things we want to do

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.240
if we don't have our health.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.480
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.680
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.406
Did you know that billions are spent
on glucosamine supplements every year?

00:00:30.406 --> 00:00:33.480
Well, do they work?
Are they safe?

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.720
Let's find out.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.360
Global sales
of glucosamine supplements

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.880
is estimated at $2 billion.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.520
Glucosamine is a precursor
to two of the major components

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:45.680
of cartilage,

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.160
though at the marginal
blood levels

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.480
achieved by supplementation,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.720
one would not expect it
to contribute much

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.360
to cartilage formation directly.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.360
There are marked inconsistencies

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.160
in the clinical research
literature

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.640
as to whether it works at all.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:03.040
The most potent predictor
of trial results?

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.600
Industry funding.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.400
Studies sponsored
by the product makers themselves

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.800
showed that their patented
products were beneficial,

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.200
but independently-funded studies

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.720
showed glucosamine
had no effect.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.400
This has raised
serious concerns

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.520
about "publication bias,"

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.760
the suspicion
that the glucosamine industry

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.560
quietly shelved rather than
published any studies

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:25.840
that didn't go their way

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.360
to give an overly rosy picture
in the medical literature.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.480
This is what led in part

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.040
to the current American College
of Rheumatology guidelines

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.080
strongly recommending against
the use of glucosamine.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.040
The proscription
against glucosamine

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.840
is echoed by some expert
consensus guidelines,

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.640
for example, the American
Academy of Orthopedic Surgeons

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.920
and Osteoarthritis
Research Society International,

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.760
but not others,
such as the European Society

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.440
for Clinical
and Economic Aspects

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.080
of Osteoporosis,
Osteoarthritis,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.360
and Musculoskeletal Diseases,
which allows an exception

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:02.000
for pharmaceutical-grade
glucosamine.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.600
Only this patented so-called
"crystalline" glucosamine

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.240
sold as a prescription-only drug
in Europe

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:08.440
has been decisively shown

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.720
to improve osteoarthritic
joint pain or function,

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.240
whereas the over-the-counter
glucosamine supplements

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.520
sold in the U.S.
offered mixed results

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.640
with no overall effect,

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.440
presumably because of
quality control analyses

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.400
by Consumer Reports and others

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.600
found glucosamine supplements
sometimes contained

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.720
no glucosamine at all.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.400
An investigation of over
a dozen glucosamine supplements

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:35.120
found that only one contained
the claimed dose on the label.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.520
So, maybe the inconsistency
in findings

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.960
is less a matter
of funding bias

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.960
and more a reflection
of the efficacy

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.720
of using genuine glucosamine.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.400
I'd feel more confident
in the industry results

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.880
if they were more transparent

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.040
with their participant-level
results.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.800
A request for data sharing was
reportedly denied by the owner

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.120
of the crystalline
glucosamine trials,

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.920
which "raises concerns

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.400
about the robustness
of their study findings."

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.000
Regardless, the effect size
of the pain relief

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.040
found even in the best studies
of crystalline glucosamine

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.920
can be considered
relatively small.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.160
Effect size can be quantified

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.520
as a "standardized
mean difference."

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:19.440
An effect size of 0.2
is considered small,

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.320
0.5 moderate, and 0.8 large.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.720
The effect size
of the best studies

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.240
on crystalline glucosamine,
0.27,

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.000
representing a small effect.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.080
So, prescription glucosamine
works better than Tylenol,

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.320
but on par
with placebo injections

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.320
and less than NSAID drugs
like ibuprofen.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.160
Now, glucosamine is safer
than NSAIDs,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.120
but the tantalizing possibility

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.840
is that it could offer more
than just symptomatic relief.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:52.280
Two industry-funded
randomized controlled trials

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.280
found that those
with knee osteoarthritis

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.680
randomized to take
the prescription glucosamine

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:57.920
for three years

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.480
experienced less progression
of their disease

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.560
compared to placebo,

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.200
as quantified
by X-ray measurements.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.120
Those on the glucosamine
had a 62 percent reduction

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.440
in osteoarthritis progression

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.680
as measured
by joint space narrowing

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.280
compared to those randomized
instead to placebo.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.040
However, two subsequent
non-industry-funded studies

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.760
found no benefit

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.920
on osteoarthritis disease
progression,

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.800
resulting in no benefit overall

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:26.880
when all four studies
were combined.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.920
But how's this for a purported
potential side effect:

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.960
a longer life?

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.480
Glucosamine supplementation
extends the lifespan

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:38.880
of both microscopic worms
and aging mice.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.880
What about people?

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.000
In 2012, the Vitamins
and Lifestyle cohort

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.880
was the first to report
on the relationship

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.760
between glucosamine use
and mortality.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.480
About 75,000
Washington State residents

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:53.960
aged 50 through 76
were followed

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.320
for about seven years,

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:58.760
and those taking glucosamine
were 18 percent less likely

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.880
to die in that period.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.880
In 2020,
two other cohort studies

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:03.920
were published on the matter,

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:06.760
including the enormous
UK Biobank study

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.480
that followed nearly
a half million people

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:10.080
for nine years.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.920
Glucosamine users were
15 percent less likely to die,

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.160
and in a 2020
national U.S. study,

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.560
users had 27 percent lower risk
of death.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.520
Since glucosamine use
has been associated

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.480
with lower CRP blood levels,
researchers suggested

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:27.840
this may be
an anti-inflammatory effect,

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.760
but when actually put
to the test,

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.560
glucosamine doesn't appear
to affect CRP at all.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.200
A more likely explanation

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:38.480
may be the so-called
"healthy user effect."

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.960
Those who choose
to take supplements

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.120
tend to be healthier
than those who don't.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.120
Studies show
dietary supplement users

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:49.160
are more likely to be female,
more educated,

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.520
and make healthier
diet and lifestyle choices,

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.880
such as exercising more
and smoking less,

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.240
and being less sick.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:58.640
So, presumably, that's why
observational studies found

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.760
that those who take vitamins
may have lower mortality rates,

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.640
but when put to the test
in interventional studies,

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.800
there was no benefit or worse.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.680
One of the most dramatic
examples

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.840
of the healthy user effect

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:13.760
is the finding that elders
who take flu vaccines

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.400
appear to cut their risk
of all-cause winter mortality

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.840
by 50 percent,

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:21.440
when seasonal flu itself
rarely causes

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:24.720
more than 10 percent
of excess winter deaths.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.480
That's why randomized
controlled trials

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:29.560
are so critical to establishing
cause and effect,

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:34.680
and we have no such data
as of yet for glucosamine.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:36.720
The cohort studies
did try to adjust

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.920
for factors such as age,
obesity, exercise education,

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.040
and smoking status,

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.480
but it's not possible to control

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:46.115
for unmeasured
lifestyle confounders.

00:06:46.382 --> 00:06:47.160
In our next story,

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:51.240
we ask why some clinical guidelines
recommend chondroitin supplements

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:54.360
but others do not.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:57.800
Chondroitin is a structural
component of cartilage

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.560
commonly used
as a dietary supplement

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:03.480
for osteoarthritis
that shares a similar story

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:04.960
with glucosamine.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:07.480
There's a large heterogeneity
in outcomes,

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.240
with the industry-funded studies

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.560
showing a benefit
for symptomatic relief

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:15.240
and the non-industry-funded
studies showing no effect,

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:18.680
with a small effect size
similar to glucosamine.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:21.200
Considering just the largest,
best-run studies,

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:22.880
the benefit of chondroitin
was found to be

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.680
"minimal or nonexistent"

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:28.080
and its use "therefore
be discouraged."

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.080
Like glucosamine,

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.400
the current American College
of Rheumatology guidelines

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:32.720
"strongly recommend against"

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.920
the use of as chondroitin
for knee or hip osteoarthritis,

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:39.040
along with the American Academy
of Orthopedic Surgeons

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.600
and Osteoarthritis Research
Society International,

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.120
whereas the European Society

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.880
for Clinical
and Economic Aspects

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:46.520
of Osteoporosis,
Osteoarthritis,

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.400
and Musculoskeletal Diseases
again allow

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.800
for the use
of pharmaceutical-grade,

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:54.240
prescription-only chondroitin.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.440
Chondroitin is
typically extracted

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:59.600
from animal cartilage-
shark fins, bovine,

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:02.880
and chicken windpipes,
or pig noses-

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.640
and slaughterhouse
supply chains

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:08.160
are not known for their "good
manufacturing practices."

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:10.920
The lack of purity
and presence of contaminants

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:14.600
is blamed in part for the lack
of consistent reproducibility.

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:17.040
A study of 32 chondroitin
supplements on the market

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.520
found that only five
contained the labeled amount,

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.600
and some contained none.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:24.800
Terms like "quality tested"
or retail price

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:27.640
were found to provide no basis
for judging quality.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.000
Some of the cheapest

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.320
and the most expensive
chondroitin on the market

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:35.000
contained less than 10 percent
actual chondroitin.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.840
When the National
Institutes of Health

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:39.160
set out to design
the esteemed GAIT trial,

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:42.560
the Glucosamine/Chondroitin
Arthritis Intervention Trial,

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:45.080
they ruled out
20 different commercial products

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.440
for issues like quality control
before giving up

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:50.840
and just deciding to have it
specially made themselves.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.800
More than 1500 patients

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.760
with symptomatic
knee osteoarthritis

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:55.840
were randomized to take

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:59.440
standard daily doses
of glucosamine, chondroitin,

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:02.120
both glucosamine
and chondroitin,

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.400
an NSAID
anti-inflammatory drug,

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.040
or a placebo for six months.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:10.840
Only the drug beat out placebo
for pain management.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.760
Neither glucosamine
and chondroitin alone

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:15.880
or in combination
reduced pain effectively,

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:18.360
and neither did it have
any significant effect

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:21.560
on delaying disease progression
on X-ray.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.280
Chondroitin also failed
in a two-year study,

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.600
but two other trials
found that by year two

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:28.440
objective benefits
could be found,

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:31.680
and a third using
more sensitive imaging (MRI)

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:33.120
could pick up
protective effects

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:34.480
by six months.

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:35.640
If you want to give it a try,

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.720
there's now
a purified non-animal source

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.320
of chondroitin
made from scratch

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:42.480
that should be free
of contaminants.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:45.480
In the U.S., chondroitin
and glucosamine

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.520
are almost always sold
in a combination pill.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:51.280
Like in the GAIT trial,
a meta-analysis of studies

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.240
pitting both
against osteoarthritis

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:56.960
found no clinically significant
benefit.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:59.320
However, there had
never been a trial

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.480
in which pharmaceutical-grade,

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:05.200
prescription-only preparations
of both were used together

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:08.640
until finally
one was published in 2017.

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.760
The multicenter
randomized, double-blind,

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:12.080
placebo-controlled
clinical trial

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:14.320
had to be stopped prematurely

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:17.400
because one group was doing
so much better than the other

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:20.264
that it was deemed unethical
to continue.

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:25.280
But that superior treatment
was the placebo!

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:27.720
Unexpectedly,
when the code was broken,

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:31.240
it turned out that
the placebo group did better!

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:32.280
In other words,

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:34.760
the industry-funded study
found that their own

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:37.000
pharmaceutical-grade
chondroitin/glucosamine

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.360
was making the pain
significantly worse

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:40.920
compared to a sugar pill.

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:43.320
In the sugar pill group,
47 percent had

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:44.840
at least a 50 percent
improvement

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:45.600
in pain or function,

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:47.520
compared to just 28 percent

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:49.880
in the chondroitin/glucosamine
group.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:53.160
What the chondroitin/glucosamine
users did get

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:54.240
was more side effects,

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:56.400
such as diarrhea
and abdominal pain;

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.160
so, doctors may want
to tell their patients

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:00.720
to stop taking their glucosamine
and chondroitin

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:06.002
as it is less effective
than placebo.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:08.720
